{"id":"word:hebrew:H8074","type":"word","title":"שָׁמֵם","subtitle":"H8074 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to stun (or intransitively, grow numb ), i.e. devastate or (figuratively) stupefy (both usually in a passive sense)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁמֵם (H8074) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 86 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁמֵם (shâmêm) means to stun (or intransitively, grow numb ), i.e. devastate or (figuratively) stupefy (both usually in a passive sense) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 9 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁמֵם","transliteration":"shâmêm","pronunciation":"shaw-mame'","strong":"H8074","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8074","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/נָשַׁ֨מּוּ֙","יִשֹּׁ֥ם","שֹׁמֵמֽוֹת","מְשׁוֹמֵֽם","שָׁמְמ֖וּ"],"morphs":[["HVqi3ms",6],["HC/VNq3cp",6],["HC/Vhq1cs",6],["HVNp3cp",5],["HVNrfpa",4],["HVqp3cp",4],["HVHc/Sp3fs",3],["HVqrmsa",3],["HC/Vqq3cp",3],["HTd/VNsfsa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to stun (or intransitively, grow numb ), i.e. devastate or (figuratively) stupefy (both usually in a passive sense)","usage":"make amazed, be astonied, (be an) astonish(-ment), (be, bring into, unto, lay, lie, make) desolate(-ion, places), be destitute, destroy (self), (lay, lie, make) waste, wonder.","full":"H8074. shamem [ שָׁמֵם ] verb be desoleted, appalled (connection of meanings not clear) (Late Hebrew id .; Jewish-Aramaic שְׁמַם Ithpe`el be dazed ); — Qal Perfect 3feminine singular שָׁמֵ֑מָה Ezek 35:15 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשֹּׁם ; 1Kin 9:8 +, 3 masculine plural יָשֹּׁ֫מּוּ Job 17:8 ; Psa 40:16 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural שֹׁ֫מוּ Jer 2:19 ; Infinitive construct (?) metaplastic שַׁמוֺת Ezek 36:3 (Ges § 67r , but see infra); — תֵּשַׁם , etc. (see [ יָשַׁם ]) are placed here by most; 6:6 reads תִּישָׁ֑מְנָה , see Ges § 67 p dd; — Participle שׁוֺמֵם Lam 3:11 (see also Po- .); feminine שֹׁמֵמָ֔ה (Ges § 84a s) 2Sam 13:20 +; plural שׁוֺמֵמִין Lam 1:14 , etc.; &#8212; 1 be desolated , of Tamar 2Sam 13:20 (i.e. deflowered, or deserted; others appalled ), of person elsewhere late Lam 1:16 ; שֹׁמֵמָה נְתָנַנִי 1:13 , שׁ ׳שָׂמַ֫נִי 3:11 ; participle as feminine noun שׁוֺמֵמָה בְּנֵי Isa 54:1 (opposed to בְּעוּלָה ) [ Dan 8:13 +? Po- .]; usually of land, etc. (sometimes= deserted ), Isa 49:8 ; Ezek 33:28 ( עוֺבֵר מֵאֵין ), 35:12 (read שָֽׁמְמוּ Qr Co Toy Krae; &gt;Kt שׁממה ), 35:15 ; הַשֹּׁמִמוֺת הֶחְָרָבוֺת 36:4 (|| שַׁמּוֺת הַנֱּעֶזָבוֺת הֶעָרִים ) 36:3 is probably corrupt, Co שְׁאָט as 36:5 , Hi-Sm from שׁמה = נשׁם , Toy reads נָשֹׁם , Krae נָשֹׁם ; — participle feminine plural as noun = desolate places Isa 49:19 ; 61:4 (both || חֳרָבוֺת ), 61:4 (compare שְׁמָמָה 62:4 ); = desolations Dan 9:18 , 26 . 2 be appalled, awestruck , usually at ( עַל ) judgments on others, Lev 26:32 (H), Jer 2:12 (see II. [ חָרֵב ]), Ezek 26:16 ; 27:35 ; 28:19 ; Isa 52:14 ; Job 17:8 , compare 1Kin 9:8 2Chr 7:12 ; Jer 18:16 ; 19:8 ; 49:17 ; 50:13 ; on oneself Psa 40:16 ( עַלעֵֿקֶב ). — Isa 42:14 see [ נשׁם ]. Niph`al Perfect 3feminine singular נָשַׁ֫מָּה Jer 12:11 +, 3 plural נָשַׁ֫נּוּ Zeph 3:6 +; Participle feminine נְשַׁמָּה Ezek 36:34 +, etc.; — = Qal: 1. be desolated , of roads Lev 26:22 (H), Isa 33:8 , bamoth Amos 7:9 (|| יֶחֱרָ֑בוּ ), altars Ezek 6:4 ; compare 25:3 ; 32:15 ; Zeph 3:6 ; Zech 7:14 ; Joel 1:17 ; Psa 69:26 ; of lands Ezek 29:12 ; 30:7 ; 36:34-35 , cities Isa 54:3 (opposed to יוֺשִׁיבוּ ), compare Ezek 36:35 ; Amos 9:14 ; Jer 33:10 ; הַנְּשַׁמָּה Ezek 36:36 the desolated (that is, land, in figure). 2 be appalled Jer 4:9 ; Lam 4:5 ; Ezek 4:17 ; 30:7 , with עַל of thing Job 18:20 . Po` Participle 1 מְשׁוֺמֵם וֵָאשְׁבָה Ezra 9:3 I sat appalled , compare 9:4 2 transitive appalling, causing horror (Dr Dan 150 f. ): מְשֹׁמֵם (הַ)שִּׁקּוּץ Dan 11:31 , + perhaps 9:27 a (see שִׁקּוּץ ); so also ׳שִׁוּ שֹׁמֵם 12:11 (on ׳שׁ v, Ges § 52s ), שֹׁמֵם הַמֶּשַׁע 8:13 the crime causing horror , and ׳שׁ as noun horror-causer, appaller , 9:27 b. Hiph`il Perfect 2masculine singular הֲשִׁמּ֫וֺתָ Job 16:7 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יַשּׁים (Ges § 67y ) Jer 49:20 ; 50:45 , 3 masculine plural suffix וַיְשִׁמֵּם 1Sam 5:6 , 1 plural נַשִּׁים Num 21:30 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural הָשַׁמּוּ (Ges § 67v ) Job 21:5 ; Infinitive absolute הַשְׁמֵם Micah 6:13 ; Participle מַשְׁמִים Ezek 3:15 ; &#8212; 1 devastate, ravage , accusative of person 1Sam 5:6 ; Ezek 20:26 ; Hosea 2:14 (figurative of vine), Job 16:7 ; accusative of location Lev 26:31-32 , (H) Jer 10:25 ; Ezek 30:12 , 14 ; Psa 79:7 , so (accusative omitted) Num 21:30 (poem in J E), Micah 6:13 ; &#8212; Ezek 14:8 see שִׂים Hiph`il 2. a. appal , accusative of person, with עַל at , Jer 49:20 ; 50:45 ; Ezek 32:10 . b. inwardly transitive , ׳מִשׁ וָאֵשֵׁב Ezek 3:15 shewing horror , Job 21:5 (Bu Niph`al הִשַּׁמוּ ). Hoph`al Infinitive construct הָשַּׁמָּה כָּליְֿמֵי (that is הָאָרֶץ ) Lev 26:34 (H) all the days of (its) being desolate , so 26:35 ; 2Chr 36:21 ; Aramaizing, בָּהְשַׁמָּה (Ges § 67y ) Lev 26:43 . Hithpo`el Imperfect 3masculine singular יִשְׁתּוֺמֵם Psa 143:4 , etc.; &#8212; 1 be appalled, astounded , כִּי that, because , Isa 59:16 ; 63:5 ; עַל of thing Dan 8:27 ; יִשְׁתּ ׳עבּתוֺכִי Psa 143:4 (compare 1 plural נשתומם Ecclus. 43:24). 2 cause oneself desolation, ruin , Eccl 7:16 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 9 8","keyReferences":["1Kgs 9 8","1Sam 5 6","2Chr 7 21","2Chr 36 21","Amos 7 9","Amos 9 14","Dan 8 13","Dan 8 27"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":86,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 9 8","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִשֹּׁ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 5 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":5,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְשִׁמֵּ֑/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"H